h=A.d([A.h(a4,a4,A.e(c,a4,a4,h,a4,12,A.b().gh().gi().x,B.a,0,a4,!1),a8),A.h(a4,a4,A.f().$0(),'\nVisit the fascinating city of Dubai. We will start the circuit by seeing the\xa0Governor\'s palace\xa0and the historic\xa0Bastakiya\xa0neighbourhood, a reproduction of the old neighbourhood with the old houses and the well-known wind towers.\xa0Fort Al Fahidi\xa0transports us some 210 years back, and is where we find the current Dubai Museum. Then we will cross the Dubai Creek with the \u201cAbra\u201d, the famous water taxi, before visiting the spice and gold markets. Later we will make a stop at the "Union House", continuing to the\xa0Jumeirah Mosque\xa0where we will stop to take some photos. We will continue along the sunny Jumeirah Beach to see the symbol of the city, the "Burj Al Arab" hotel in Dubai. Later we will drive through the Palm Island and we will stop to take a photo in front of the largest Hotel in the entire Middle East, the \u201cAtlantis\u201d hotel. Next we will drive through Sheikh Zayed Road, from where we will be able to appreciate the great skyscrapers of the city, where the business area is located. We will stop in the center of the new area of \u200b\u200bthe city, Downtown, where the tallest tower in the world is located, the "Burj Khalifa" next to the impressive Dubai Mall.\u2028Lunch not included.\nIn the afternoon we will leave for the visit of\xa0Sharjah, an emirate near Dubai. The first visit we will make will be at the\xa0University of Sharjah, inaugurated in 1998. From there we will go to the \u201cCultural Rotunda\u201d where we can take photos of the Mosque. We will stop at the Blue Mall in Sharjah where you will have the option to haggle on your purchases of gold, electronics, etc. Then we will visit the\xa0Souq-Al-Masqoof, an old part of the city that was covered and serves as a shopping area. Return to Dubai.\u2028Accommodation in Dubai.')],d)
