g=A.d([A.h(a0,a0,A.f().$1$fontSize(12),"Warangal Fort was initially built by King Ganapatideva, the ruler of the Kakatiya Dynasty, in the 13th century. It was later expanded and completed by his daughter, Rani Rudrama Devi, who is known for her leadership and military acumen. The fort has witnessed numerous battles and invasions over the centuries, particularly during the decline of the Kakatiya Empire when it fell to the Tughlaqs in 1323.\n\nThe fort\u2019s design and layout were meticulously planned to provide maximum defense, with its three-layered fortified walls serving as a formidable barrier against invaders. Although parts of the fort were destroyed by invaders, the ruins still showcase the incredible craftsmanship of the Kakatiya period.")],j)
