h=A.d([A.h(d,d,A.q(d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,!0,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d),"Akshardham Temple, located along the River Yamuna in Delhi, is a breathtaking architectural masterpiece and a must-visit destination in the city. Covering 100 acres, the temple is a symbol of unity in diversity, blending various architectural styles from across India. Its grandeur earned it a spot in the Guinness Book of World Records as the World's Largest Comprehensive Hindu Temple. More than a lakh visitors come to this temple every week.\n\n\nSurrounded by stunning gardens and fountains, every aspect of Akshardham Temple showcases intricate beauty. It closely resembles the Akshardham Temple in Gandhinagar, Gujarat, in terms of design. The temple's walls are adorned with exquisite carvings of dancers, animals, gods, and musicians, showcasing the craftsmanship of ancient Indian architecture.\n\n\nInaugurated in 2005 by Pramukh Swami Maharaj of the Bochasanwasi Aksharpurushottam Swaminarayan Sanstha (BAPS), the temple was constructed with an investment of Rs 2 million. The highlight of the temple is a 141-foot-high statue of Swaminarayan, surrounded by the images of his Gurus. The complex also features a musical fountain and an IMAX theatre, adding to its charm.\n\n\nThe temple's architecture is a marvel, with 9 ornate domes, 20 quadrangle shikhars, over 20,000 statues, and intricate floral motifs. Made from Italian marble and pink sandstone, the structure was built without using any steel. Designed based on ancient Vedic principles, the temple houses the Yagnapurush Kund, India's largest step well, complete with a musical fountain. A notable feature of the temple is its Mandovar, an external wall measuring 611 ft by 31 ft, which is the largest of its kind.\n\n\nVisitors can also enjoy a delightful boat ride on an artificial river, making the experience even more memorable. Akshardham Temple is not just a religious site, but a stunning testament to India's architectural brilliance, drawing tourists from all over the world.\n")],t.R)
