h=A.d([A.h(d,d,A.q(d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,!0,d,d,d,d,d,d,d,d),'Surajkund Village, located just 20 km from the heart of Delhi, is a charming tourist destination set against the scenic backdrop of the Aravali Hills. The name "Surajkund" translates to "reservoir of the Sun," which refers to an ancient 10th-century reservoir located within the village. It is believed that this reservoir was built by a Rajput King.\n\n\nThe village offers a peaceful, rustic ambiance, making it an ideal spot to unwind. The reservoir itself is shaped like a rising sun with an eastward arc and is surrounded by a semi-circular embankment made of stepped stones. During the monsoon season, the tank is filled with water, enhancing its beauty. Most of the local population is involved in agriculture or cattle rearing, allowing visitors to explore the village and experience the rich cultural heritage of the area.\n\n\nSurajkund also offers accommodation options, making it an excellent place for a peaceful stay away from the hustle and bustle of city life. You can wake up to the soothing sounds of birds and enjoy the tranquility of the surroundings. The nearby forest is home to a wide variety of flora and fauna, adding to the charm of this picturesque spot. It is a popular picnic destination for Delhi residents.\n\n\nThe main attraction of Surajkund Village is the annual Surajkund Craft Mela, organized by Haryana Tourism every February. This two-week fair brings together artists, weavers, sculptors, and craftsmen from all over India and neighboring countries. Visitors can enjoy live traditional dance and music performances, with puppet shows being one of the highlights. The fair features around 400 stalls selling a wide variety of handicrafts, making it a perfect place to explore and buy unique items.\n')],t.R)
