g=A.d([A.h(a2,a2,A.f().$0(),"The influence of Portuguese rule in Goa has left an indelible mark on the state\u2019s cultural and religious practices. The majority of Goa\u2019s population is Christian, and they celebrate various Christian festivals with immense joy and enthusiasm. Homes and churches are decorated with colorful lights, flowers, and Christmas trees during the festive seasons. Some of the most popular Christian festivals in Goa are:\n\nGood Friday & Easter: Celebrated with solemn religious services and processions, marking the crucifixion and resurrection of Christ.\n\nMargao Feast: Held in honor of the patron saint of Margao, Saint Jerome, this feast is accompanied by church services, processions, and communal feasting.\n\nSt. Xavier\u2019s Feast: Held in Old Goa at the Basilica of Bom Jesus, this feast celebrates the life of St. Francis Xavier, with special masses and processions.\n\nChristmas: Christmas in Goa is a grand celebration, with churches hosting midnight masses and homes illuminated with festive decorations. The entire state takes on a magical charm with Christmas trees and carol singing.\n")],j)
