f=A.d([A.h(a,a,A.f().$0(),"One of the most fascinating and energetic dance forms of Gujarat, Dandiya Raas is especially popular during the Navratri festival. This dance is celebrated not only in Gujarat but also across the country, as it forms an essential part of the festival, which honors the nine manifestations of the Mother Goddess. During Navratri, devotees fast, offer prayers, and participate in joyous dance performances, with Dandiya Raas taking center stage in the evening celebrations.\n\nThe dance involves men and women dressed in colorful traditional attire, using beautifully decorated wooden sticks (called dandiyas) as props. These bamboo sticks are painted in bright colors and are rhythmically struck together on the beats of the music. The dancers move in a circular formation, striking their sticks in time with the music, creating a vibrant display of energy and rhythm.\n\nThe music, usually accompanied by instruments like the dhol, is fast-paced and demands great energy. The dance is known for its joyful spirit and the way it brings communities together. The Kathiawari Raas dancers of Gujarat are particularly renowned for their exceptional skill in Dandiya Raas.")],i)
