f=A.d([A.h(a4,a4,A.f().$0(),"famous lake in the region. Stretching over 15.5 km, Dal Lake is a visual masterpiece, with its floating houseboats, intricate Mughal gardens, and bustling markets. The sight of shikaras (traditional wooden boats) drifting through the lake, with the backdrop of snow-capped mountains, is a postcard-perfect scene. The lake is also home to beautiful lotus flowers, especially during the blooming months of July and August. Dal Lake is divided into two parts\u2014Bod Lake (the larger part) and Lokut Lake (the smaller part), each offering its own charm.\n\nIn winter, when the temperature drops to -11\xb0C, the lake freezes, and children can be seen playing on the ice. Dal Lake is a must-visit on every Kashmir itinerary, whether you're looking for peace or adventure.")],h)
