g=A.d([A.h(a0,a0,A.q(a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,!0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0),"Mattupetty Dam\nLocated 13 km from Munnar, this concrete gravity dam is set amidst rolling hills. It serves as a storage facility for hydroelectric projects and is a great spot to enjoy serene natural surroundings. The nearby waterholes are frequented by elephants, adding to the charm.\nMattupetty Indo-Swiss Dairy Farm\nThis unique dairy farm is part of the Indo-Swiss Livestock Project, where high-breed cattle and innovative varieties are developed. Visitors can learn about advanced dairy farming techniques.\nKundala Lake\nAn artificial reservoir 20 km from Munnar, Kundala Lake is surrounded by lush valleys and majestic landscapes. A Shikara boat ride on this tranquil lake is a must for visitors.\nTop Station\nSituated 40 km from Munnar at an altitude of 1,880 meters, Top Station offers panoramic views of the Western Ghats and the Theni Valley. It is a prime location to witness the blooming Neelakurinji flowers.\nEcho Point\nLocated 15 km from Munnar, Echo Point is a unique destination where your voice echoes back to you. It's a favorite spot for nature photography and an ideal location for some playful fun.\nRajamalai (Eravikulam National Park)\nPart of Eravikulam National Park, Rajamalai is home to the endangered Nilgiri Tahr and features rare orchids and rich biodiversity. It's a haven for nature enthusiasts and trekkers.\nTea Museum\nThis museum, located in the KDHP\u2019s Nullatanni estate, is one of a kind in India. It offers insights into the history and process of tea cultivation, making it a delightful experience for tea lovers.\nMarayoor Sandalwood Forests\nFamous for its sandalwood forests, Marayoor also holds historical significance, with remnants of Stone Age civilization, including dolmens, rock edicts, and paintings dating back to 10,000 B.C.\nAttukad Waterfalls\nThis picturesque waterfall is located 9 km from Munnar, en route to Pallivasal. Its beauty is most captivating after the monsoon season.\nLakkom Waterfalls\nSituated about 25 km from Munnar, these cascading falls are part of the Eravikulam National Park. Their scenic surroundings make them a popular destination.")],j)
