h=A.d([A.h(d,d,A.f().$0(),"The snake boat races of Kerala are an exhilarating and mesmerizing experience, filled with excitement and adventure. These globally renowned events draw spectators from across India and the world every year. Once a year, the tranquil backwaters of Kerala burst into life, creating a vibrant and festive atmosphere during these thrilling races. The enthusiasm of Kerala's village communities is infectious, and for them, participating in the snake boat races is a matter of immense pride.\n\nThe traditional boats used in these races, called chunduvalloms, are masterpieces of craftsmanship. Crafted from massive tree trunks, these boats are transformed into vibrant, snake-shaped regattas, with their prows designed to resemble open snake jaws.\n\nEach chunduvallom can accommodate over 100 oarsmen, showcasing the incredible teamwork and spirit of the participants.\n\nSome of the most celebrated snake boat races include the Nehru Trophy Boat Race, Aranmula Snake Boat Race, Rajiv Gandhi Boat Race, Champakulam Moolam Snake Boat Race, Payippad Boat Race, and Pamba Snake Boat Race. These events add a splash of color and energy to the lush green backwaters of Kerala, creating unforgettable memories for all who witness them.")],t.R)
