g=A.d([A.h(a4,a4,A.q(a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,!0,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4),"Khajuraho, located in the heart of Madhya Pradesh, is renowned worldwide for its exceptional temple architecture and intricate sculptures. Surrounded by the lush, forested plains of Bundelkhand, Khajuraho is a testament to the artistic and cultural legacy of India. The temples, built between the 9th and 11th centuries by the Chandela dynasty, remain a marvel even after over a thousand years. Though the exact reason behind the massive scale of temple construction remains a mystery, local legend suggests that the first Chandela king constructed these temples to atone for his mother\u2019s sin, as she had a celestial union with the Moon God, which marked the beginning of the Chandela dynasty.\n\nKhajuraho is a blend of history, culture, architecture, and environment, offering a tranquil escape from the noise and pollution of urban life. Its serene landscapes, combined with the magnificent temples, make it one of the most famous tourist destinations in India. Visitors can also partake in the annual Shivaratri fair, which celebrates the divine wedding of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati.")],j)
