g=A.d([A.h(a0,a0,A.f().$0(),'Temples\nThe Sun Temple, also known as the "Black Pagoda," is the city\'s centerpiece, drawing visitors from around the world. This architectural marvel is designed as a massive chariot dedicated to the Sun God, adorned with 24 intricately carved wheels and horses. A UNESCO World Heritage Site, the temple is renowned for its unmatched stone carvings and artistic brilliance.\nThe Melakkadambur Shiva Temple, dating back to the Chola dynasty, and the Ramachandi Temple, dedicated to Goddess Ramachandi, are other notable temples in Konark.\n\nChandrabhaga Beach\nThis picturesque beach offers breathtaking views and a serene environment. It is also known for its marine resources, natural deer park, and ancient Matha (monastic structure), making it a favorite spot for nature lovers.\n\nOther Attractions\nNearby locations such as Kuruma, Pipili, and Kakatpur add to the charm of Konark, offering unique experiences and glimpses into local culture and heritage.')],j)
