g=A.d([A.h(b,b,A.q(b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,!0,b,b,b,b,b,b,b,b),"Cattle Trading\n The fair is most renowned for its cattle trading, with camels, horses, cows, goats, and sheep paraded for sale. Visitors can witness bargaining and see beautiful, decorated animals of various breeds. Pushkar Fair is considered the world's largest camel fair, attracting cattle owners from across Rajasthan.\nCompetitions\n One of the unique features of the fair are the entertaining cattle competitions, such as the \"best decorated camel\" contest and the hilarious camel race where large numbers of people try to balance on a camel's back. The crowd enjoys watching these spirited and sometimes chaotic events.\nStalls and Shopping\n The fair has numerous stalls offering items for both humans and cattle. You can find saddles, saddle-straps, cowrie strings for animals, and colorful silver jewelry, bead necklaces, patchwork textiles, and tie-dye garments for humans. Body tattoos are also a popular attraction for visitors wanting a unique souvenir.\nRecreation\n The Pushkar Fair comes alive with folk music and dance performances, as well as exhibitions, cultural shows, and movie screenings. The performances, often featuring traditional music, add to the lively atmosphere of the fair.\n2Temples\n Pushkar is home to the revered Jagat Pita Shri Brahma Mandir, one of only five Brahma temples in India. Visitors can also trek to the Savitri Temple on a hilltop, which offers panoramic views of the Pushkar Lake. Other temples, including the Varah Temple, Mahadeva Temple, and Ramavaikunth Temple, are also must-visits for spiritual seekers.\nPushkar Lake and Ghats\n The sacred Pushkar Lake is believed to cleanse the sins of a lifetime, and there are 52 bathing ghats surrounding the lake. Pilgrims travel here to bathe and offer prayers. In the evenings, the lake is illuminated with floating earthen lamps, creating a mesmerizing sight. Kartik Purnima is considered the most auspicious day to be at Pushkar for a spiritual experience.")],j)
