d=A.d([A.h(a0,a0,A.q(a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,!0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0),"Berijam Lake\n Located amidst lush greenery, Berijam Lake is a serene spot rich in flora and fauna. As a source of drinking water for nearby villages, visitors need a special permit to access the area. The tranquil environment makes it an ideal place to rejuvenate and enjoy nature.\n\n\nCoaker's Walk\n A scenic 1-kilometer pathway along the slopes of a hillock, Coaker\u2019s Walk offers panoramic views of the valleys and cloud-kissed hills. This peaceful walk is perfect for leisurely strolls and photography enthusiasts, making it one of the favorite spots in Kodaikanal.\n\n\nKodai Lake\n At the heart of Kodaikanal, Kodai Lake is a man-made, star-shaped lake offering a range of activities, such as boating, walking along its serene banks, or simply enjoying the tranquil surroundings. It\u2019s a perfect spot for birdwatching and relaxing amidst nature.\n\n\nKurinjiandavar Temple\n This temple, dedicated to Lord Murugan, is surrounded by Kurinji flowers, which bloom once every 12 years. Built in 1936 by a European lady, the temple has become a significant pilgrimage site and a captivating destination for nature lovers.\n\n\nGreen Valley View\n Known for its breathtaking panoramic views, this spot offers visitors a view of misty woodlands and a lush green valley. The serene atmosphere and tranquil weather make it a must-visit for nature lovers seeking peace and scenic beauty.\n\n\nBear Shola Falls\n A seasonal waterfall that comes alive during the monsoon, Bear Shola Falls is a peaceful retreat, especially for nature lovers and photographers. The stunning scenery and quiet surroundings make it an ideal spot for those seeking solitude.\n\n\nPillar Rocks\n These towering rock formations, surrounded by a mini garden, provide panoramic views of the surrounding region, making it a favorite for photography and picnics. The striking landscape is a beautiful sight for visitors to explore.\n\n\nDevil's Kitchen\n Located between Green Valley View and Pillar Rocks, Devil\u2019s Kitchen consists of hidden caves and rocky terrains, offering adventurous travelers a thrilling experience while exploring the mysterious landscape.")],j)
