j=A.d([A.h(e,e,A.f().$0(),"Madurai, the third largest city in Tamil Nadu, is renowned for its cultural and historical significance. Known by several names, such as the Temple City, City of Four Junctions, City of Jasmine, and City that Never Sleeps, Madurai is famous for its stunning temples and vibrant festivals. The city\u2019s temples, built by the Pandayan and Madurai Nayak kings, showcase impressive Dravidian-style architecture, drawing tourists from all over the world. As a prominent Hindu pilgrimage destination, Madurai also plays a crucial role in the nation\u2019s economy, being a major rubber producer and serving key industries.\n\nThe Meenakshi Temple, the city\u2019s most famous landmark, is a must-visit attraction, offering a captivating glimpse into Dravidian architecture. The temple is dedicated to Goddess Meenakshi and holds immense significance in Hinduism. Other notable temples include the Koodal Alagar Temple, located in the city\u2019s heart, which houses three staircases of the Lord posture; Thiruparankundram, dedicated to Lord Muruga; and Pazhamudhir Solai, an important temple dedicated to Lord Kartikeyan.\n\nApart from temples, Madurai has several other must-see attractions, including the Gorippalayam Dargah, Vandiyur Mariamman Teppakulam, Kazimar Big Mosque, Maqbara Gandhi Museum, Thirupparankundram, and Thirumalai Nayak Palace, each adding to the city\u2019s charm.\n\nMadurai welcomes tourists year-round, with the best time to visit being between October and March, when the weather is more pleasant and various festivals can be enjoyed. Accommodation options range from budget to luxury hotels, catering to different preferences and budgets.\n\nMadurai is well-connected by air, road, and rail. The Madurai Domestic Airport is primarily connected to Chennai and other major cities in India, while international travelers can use the Trichy International Airport. The city is situated on a national highway, making it accessible by state and private bus services from nearby cities. The railway network is also extensive, with regular services linking Madurai to important cities across the country.")],t.R)
