e=A.d([A.h(a,a,A.q(a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,!0,a,a,a,a,a,a,a,a),"Doddabetta Peak\n Doddabetta Peak, the highest point in the Nilgiri district, offers stunning panoramic views that are hard to rival. Known for its incredible beauty, the location is a favorite among tourists and is especially romantic. Honeymooners often visit to enjoy the breathtaking scenery and capture the moment in photographs.\n\n\nOoty Botanical Gardens\n The Government Botanical Gardens, established in 1847, spans over 22 hectares and showcases a wide variety of plants, with around 650 species in total. The garden is well-maintained and a treat for nature lovers. Among its highlights is the fossil of a tree believed to be over 20 million years old, offering visitors a glimpse into the distant past.\n\n\nAnnamalai Temple\n Dedicated to Lord Muruga, this temple holds both religious and scenic significance. It is believed to be the seventh hill temple of the lord, offering stunning views of the surrounding landscape. The temple is not only a spiritual retreat but also a popular spot for honeymooners, who seek blessings for their new life together.\n\n\nWax Museum\n The Wax Museum, funded privately, is a must-visit attraction in Ooty. Housed in a 142-year-old bungalow, it features life-size wax statues of notable figures that captivate visitors with their realism. The museum provides a unique experience and adds to the charm of the Ooty tour.\n\n\nOther Attractions\n In addition to the aforementioned sites, Ooty has several other must-visit locations. These include the Ooty Rose Garden, St. Stephen's Church, Ooty Golf Course, Tribal Museum, Ooty Mountain Railway, Toda Huts, Stone House, Ooty Lake, Sims Park in Coonoor, and the Tea Factory, each offering a distinct charm and unique experience.")],i)
