g=A.d([A.h(a0,a0,A.q(a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,!0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0,a0),"Bharat Kala Museum\n Established in 1920, Bharat Kala Museum is one of BHU\u2019s most important attractions. The museum is renowned for its vast collection of miniature paintings, sculptures, manuscripts, and archaeological artifacts, offering a glimpse into India\u2019s rich artistic history. Housing over 100,000 antiquities, including items as old as the 12th century, the museum preserves the cultural heritage of India. Mahatma Gandhi himself was impressed by the museum\u2019s collection, adding to its prestige.\n\nSayaji Rao Gaekwad Library\n The Sayaji Rao Gaekwad Library, also known as the Central Library of BHU, is a treasure trove of knowledge, containing over 1.3 million volumes of books and journals. Established in 1917 and built in 1941, the library\u2019s design was inspired by the British Museum. It is renowned for its manuscript conservation efforts and has been a part of the National Manuscripts Mission since 1941, making it an essential academic resource for students and researchers.\n\nShri Vishwanath Mandir\n Situated at the heart of BHU, the Shri Vishwanath Mandir is a striking temple with a 77-meter-high spire. Built over 30 years and completed in 1931, the temple is a blend of seven smaller temples. It holds cultural and spiritual significance for both students and locals and hosts daily rituals, musical recitals, and performances. The temple is surrounded by shops selling religious souvenirs, handicrafts, and Banarasi sarees, making it a must-visit spot for those exploring Varanasi. Nearby restaurants also offer vegetarian delicacies, enhancing the temple experience.")],j)
