g=A.d([A.h(a0,a0,A.f().$0(),"Bright End Corner\n Located just 2 kilometers from the city, Bright End Corner offers stunning views of both sunrise and sunset. This peaceful spot is perfect for a tranquil escape, and visitors can also explore the nearby Swami Vivekananda Library and ashram.\n\nNanda Devi Temple\n Situated above the Mall Road, Nanda Devi Temple is one of the most sacred temples in the Kumaon region. Dedicated to the patron goddess of the Chand Dynasty, it is over 1000 years old and features intricate stone carvings and a stunning wooden roof. The temple is a popular destination during the Nanda Devi Fair in September.\n\nChitai Temple\n This historical temple is dedicated to Gollu Devta, an avatar of Lord Shiva. Located in the town's main market, it is one of the most revered temples in Almora.\n\nGovind Ballabh Pant Public Museum\n Named after the prominent freedom fighter, this museum is located on Mall Road. It houses artifacts from the Katyuri and Chand emperors' reigns, along with Kumauni paintings that narrate the region's legends and history.\n\nZero Point\n A 2-hour trek from Almora, Zero Point is located within the Binsar Wildlife Sanctuary. Offering spectacular views of mountain peaks like Nanda Devi and Kedarnath, it\u2019s an excellent spot for nature lovers to witness a magnificent sunrise.\n\nJageshwar Shiv Temple\n Located in a pilgrimage town near Almora, Jageshwar Shiv Temple is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva. The temple complex, which includes 124 small and large stone temples, is well-preserved by the Archaeological Survey of India.\n\nKatarmal Sun Temple\n Located in a remote village near Almora, Katarmal is home to a 9th-century Sun Temple. Surrounded by 44 smaller temples, the area offers picturesque views of nature.\n\nLakhudiyar\n A prehistoric site located along the River Suyal, Lakhudiyar is known for its ancient caves with red, black, and white inscriptions. The caves offer a glimpse into life during the Stone Age era.\n\nDeer Park\n For wildlife enthusiasts, Deer Park is a must-visit. The park houses deer, leopards, and Himalayan Black Bears, providing an ideal spot for nature lovers.")],j)
