h=A.d([A.h(c,c,A.f().$0(),'Badrinath \u2013 The Garhwal Queen\nLocated on the banks of the Alakananda River, Badrinath is nestled between the Nar and Narayan mountain ranges, with the majestic Neelkanth Peak in the background. This sacred place is often referred to as the "Garhwal Queen" and is situated at an altitude of 3133 meters above sea level in the Chamoli district. The primary attraction is the Badrinath Temple, dedicated to Lord Vishnu. Pilgrims take a holy dip in the Tapt Kund before entering the temple, and the Brahma Kapal, located on the banks of the Alakananda, is a site for performing rites for departed souls.\n\nKedarnath \u2013 The Jyotirlinga\nKedarnath is situated in the Uttar Kashi district of Uttaranchal, at an altitude of 3583 meters. The Kedarnath Temple, built by the Pandavas, is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas and an important site for pilgrims. The temple offers a stunning view of the Kedardome Peak, while the Samadhi of Adiguru Shankaracharya is a significant attraction. The nearby Bhairavnath Temple, Gauri Kund, and the Chorabari Tal Lake are also visited by devotees.\n\nGangotri \u2013 The Origin of Bhagirathi\nLocated in the Garhwal Hills of Uttaranchal, Gangotri sits at an altitude of 3048 meters. The Gangotri Temple is dedicated to Goddess Ganga, and pilgrims visit to take a dip in the Bhagirathi River. The Jalamagna Shivling, visible only during winters, and Gaumukh, the glacier that marks the origin of the Ganges, are major attractions. The challenging trekking route to Nandanvan offers breathtaking views of the Shivling peak.\n\nYamunotri \u2013 The Origin of Yamuna\nYamunotri, perched at 3293 meters above sea level, is located in the Uttarkashi district and is dedicated to Goddess Yamuna. The Yamunotri Temple is the primary attraction, while Surya Kund, a thermal spring, and Divya Shilla, a sacred rock, are also important sites. The glacial lake of Saptarishi Kund, located at 4421 meters, is the actual source of the Yamuna River, and it is known for the rare Brahma lotus that grows here.')],i)
