g=A.d([A.h(a1,a1,A.q(a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,!0,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1),"Mukteshwar Temple\nThe Mukteshwar Temple is the most famous attraction in the town, located at the hilltop. The temple is known for its white marble Shivling, accompanied by a copper yoni. In addition to the idols of Parvati, Ganesh, and Nandi, the temple also houses idols of Brahma and Vishnu. The temple\u2019s calm and peaceful ambiance offers a heavenly experience for visitors.\n\nChauthi Jaali (Chauli Ka Jali)\nLocated near the Mukteshwar Temple, Chauthi Jaali is a fascinating place surrounded by local legends. According to one story, it was the site of a battle between a demon and a goddess. Another belief suggests that a barren woman crossing the hole in the rock will be blessed with a child. The area provides panoramic views and is a must-visit for all travelers.\n\nThe Rajarani Temple\nBuilt in the 11th century, the Rajarani Temple is renowned for its stunning stone carvings of female figures in various dance postures. Set amidst lush paddy fields, the temple may be small in size but its intricate carvings make it a popular tourist destination.\nBhalu Gaad Waterfall\nBhalu Gaad Waterfall is a beautiful and crystal-clear waterfall located in Mukteshwar. Known for its breathtaking beauty, the waterfall attracts trekkers and hikers. The thundering sound of the water cascading down the rocks is a sight to behold.")],j)
