g=A.d([A.h(a1,a1,A.q(a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,!0,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1),"Lakshman Jhula\nLakshman Jhula, built in 1929, is a hanging iron bridge that holds great significance in the Hindu epic. The bridge is associated with the belief that Lakshman crossed the river at this point. Visitors can enjoy spectacular views of the Ganga and surrounding mountains from the bridge.\n\nRishikund\nLocated near Triveni Ghat, Rishikund is an ancient pond believed to be blessed by Goddess Yamuna. The nearby Raghunath Temple, dedicated to Lord Rama and his wife Sita, is a popular destination for pilgrims. The Ganga Aarti at Triveni Ghat is also a must-watch for spiritual seekers.\n\nTera Manzil Temple\nThis multi-story temple offers a panoramic view of the town and the river. It is known for its stunning sunrise and sunset views, as well as for housing idols of various Hindu gods and goddesses.\n\nBharat Mandir\nSituated on the banks of the Ganges, Bharat Mandir was constructed in the 12th century by Adiguru Shankracharya. The temple is dedicated to Lord Vishnu and contains an idol made of Shaligram stone. It holds significant importance in Hindu mythology and attracts devotees, especially during Akshaya Tritiya.\n\nGeeta Bhawan\nOne of the oldest temple complexes in Rishikesh, Geeta Bhawan is famous for its beautiful illustrations of the Ramayana and Mahabharata on its walls. It is a peaceful spot for meditation and spiritual practices.\n\nRam Jhula\nA suspension bridge similar to Lakshman Jhula, Ram Jhula connects Shivanand Ashram and Sawarg Ashram. It provides a scenic view of the Ganga and the surrounding area, making it a popular spot for tourists.")],j)
