g=A.d([A.h(d,d,A.e(j,d,d,h,d,d,A.b().gh().gi().x,g.w,0,d,!1),"This sacred journey covers two of the most revered pilgrimage sites in India \u2014 Kashi and Prayag. Kashi (Varanasi), the eternal city, and Prayagraj, home to the holy Triveni Sangam, hold immense spiritual significance. It is believed that a pilgrimage to these two places leads to moksha (salvation).\n\nAccording to legend, when Lord Kartikeya met Rishi Agastya, he touched various parts of the sage\u2019s body, symbolizing reverence as though he were touching the sacred land of Kashi and Prayag.\n\nDay 1: Arrival in Kashi (Varanasi) \u2013 Spiritual Immersion\nReceive a warm welcome on arrival and transfer to the hotel for check-in.\n\nBegin your spiritual journey with visits to important temples such as Kashi Vishwanath Ji, Sankat Mochan, Durga Ji, Bharat Mata Temple, and BHU Vishwanath Ji.\n\nExplore Assi Ghat, Ramnagar Fort, and witness the mesmerizing evening Ganga Aarti.\n\nOptional: Early morning Mangal Aarti experience (starts at 2:30 AM).\n\nDay 2: Prayagraj Excursion \u2013 Triveni Sangam & Rituals\nDepart early for a day trip to Prayagraj (~2\u20133 hours by road).\n\nTake a holy dip at the sacred Triveni Sangam, where the Ganga, Yamuna, and mythical Saraswati rivers meet.\n\nPerform puja and rituals at the Sangam for spiritual cleansing.\n\nVisit other significant sites in Prayagraj before returning to Varanasi by evening.\n\nDay 3: Temple Visits & Departure\nEarly morning boating on the Ganga, followed by darshan at Kal Bhairav, Vishalakshi Ji, and Annapurna Ji, time permitting.\n\nEnjoy breakfast, check out, and proceed for onward travel.\n\nHighlights & Spiritual Sites:\nShri Kashi Vishwanath Temple (Jyotirling), Sankat Mochan, Durga Ji, Bharat Mata Temple, BHU Vishwanath Ji, Ramnagar Fort, Assi Ghat, Evening Ganga Aarti, Triveni Sangam (Prayagraj), Kal Bhairav, Vishalakshi Ji,\xa0Annapurna\xa0Ji.")],t.R)
