g=A.d([A.h(d,d,A.e(j,d,d,h,d,d,A.b().gh().gi().x,g.w,0,d,!1),"Varanasi, revered by Hindu devotees and visitors of various faiths worldwide, is a pilgrimage site encompassing Kashi, Triveni Sangam, and Gaya-Bodhgaya. Visitors perform rituals and pujas guided by ancestral traditions, believing in ancestral satisfaction and spiritual liberation. We ensure a secure and comfortable journey, welcoming Buddhist pilgrims as well.\n\nDetailed Itinerary:\n\nDay 1: Upon arrival in Varanasi, receive assistance and transfer to your hotel. In the afternoon, embark on a half-day temple tour, including visits to Mother India, Durga Temple, Tulsi Manas Temple, Sankat Mochan Temple, and New Vishwanath Temple. Experience the enchanting Ganga Aarti at Dasaswamed Ghat. Overnight at the hotel.\n\nDay 2: Begin the day with an early morning boat tour on the Ganges, exploring the bathing ghats and walking through the narrow lanes to visit the Golden Temple (Old Vishwanath Temple) and Annapurna Devi Temple. Return to the hotel for breakfast. Later, visit Kal Bhairav Temple and take an excursion to Sarnath. Return to the hotel in the afternoon. In the evening, attend a special Aarti at Vishwanath Temple (limited to 30 persons, entry fee applies) or have an ordinary Darshan. Overnight at the hotel.\n\nDay 3: After breakfast, travel to Allahabad via Vindhyachal. Visit Vindyavasini Devi Temple, Triveni Sangam at Prayag, Bade Hanuman Temple, and Anand Bhawan, before returning to Varanasi. (Optionally, opt for a day excursion to Gaya). Overnight at the hotel.\n\nDay 4: After breakfast, check out from the hotel and visit Sarnath for sightseeing. Depart from Varanasi with transfers to your onward destination.\n\nHighlighted Sites: Kashi Vishwanath Jyotirling, Kal Bhairav, Sarnath, Prayag Triveni Sangam, Vindhyachal Devi, Gaya, and Bodhgaya")],t.R)
