a9=A.d([A.h(b8,b8,A.f().$0(),"Background information: the time difference is + 5 hrs\nFrom Irkutsk to Slyudyanka, the train goes eastward without stops.\n"),A.h(b8,b8,A.q(b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,B.a,b8,b8,!0,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8),"03:03 - 06:39 - Slyudyanka "),A.h(b8,b8,A.q(b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,!0,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8)," (Tourist parking 3 hr 36 min.)\nYou can get out of the carriage and admire the world's only station building, entirely built of white and pink marble.\nThe traction will be changed during parking. On the journey from Slyudyanka to Port Baikal, the train will follow driven by a real steam locomotive.\nThose who wish will have a fascinating view of the work of the locomotive brigade when the locomotive is coupled. You will have a unique opportunity for a photo session with a steam locomotive in the background.\n"),A.h(b8,b8,A.q(b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,B.a,b8,b8,!0,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8),"06:39 \u2013"),A.h(b8,b8,A.q(b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,!0,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8),"Departure of the train in the western direction to the famous Circum-Baikal railway (your journey will be colored with a true historical flavor; you will have the opportunity to live the emotions of a person at the beginning of the 20th century and feel the regularity of that time.\nRelax time.\n\nBreakfast on board the train.\n"),A.h(b8,b8,A.q(b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,B.a,b8,b8,!0,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8),'Traveling on the Circum-Baikal railway, "the golden buckle of the steel belt of Russia" going along the shore of Lake Baikal '),A.h(b8,b8,A.q(b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,!0,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8,b8),' Is a great way to see southern Baikala and explore the architectural sights in one day. For Circum-Baikal railway uses 38 tunnels with a total length of 9,063 m (the longest of them is the 777.5 m long tunnel across Cape Polovinny), 15 stone galleries with a total length of 295 m (currently only 5 of them are used) and 3 reinforced concrete galleries with holes, 248 bridges and viaducts, 268.\n07:00 - 07:30 \u2013 station Kultuk\n07:50 - 08:20 \u2013 station Museum of the Roerichs\n09:31 - 10:01 \u2013 station Kirkirei"\n10:37 - 11:07 \u2013 station Polovinnaya\n11:29 - 11:59 \u2013 station Italianskaya stenka (Italian Wall)\nThe stopping point "Italian Wall" is adjacent to two complexes, confined to the valleys of Bolshoy and Malaya Shumikham. The first includes Cape Shumikhinsky with a tunnel and a bay, a sandy beach, a stone pipe across the river. The second consists of engineering structures: a bridge, a viaduct, a gallery and retaining walls. One of the walls - arched - "Italian", the only one, preserved in its original form, built under the leadership of the Italian citizen L. Ferrari.\n13:15 - 13:20 \u2013 station Preobrazhenskaya Church, 74 km\n13:30 \u2013 Arrival train in station Port Baikal.\nLunch on the train (for the convenience of tourists, meals are served in the compartment).\nFree time for photo shoots and relax on Lake Baikal.\nIt\'s possible to have private visit to the village of Listvyanka or a trip along the Circum-Baikal railway. The crossing is carried out in accordance with the schedule of the ferry on the route Port Baikal - Rogatka pier (Listvyanka settlement).\nPicnic on the shore of Lake Baikal.\nNight of the train')],e)
