a0=A.d([A.h(a4,a4,A.q(a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,!0,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4,a4),'Breakfast in the hotel at 09.00.\nAfter breakfast at 10.00, meet your guide at the lobby of the hotel and proceed for the walking excursion tour in Moscow.\n\nYou start the program from:\n\n- Visiting the metro and proceeding to Revolution Square metro station \u2013 where you find out what brings luck to local people and what parts of the stations the thieves prefer.\n- The Theater Square \u2013 with one of the most famous theaters in the world, The Bolshoi Theater.\nRed Square \u2013 the heart of Russia and the most famous landmark in Moscow, with a view of the Kremlin and Lenin\u2019s tomb.\n- Saint Basil\u2019s Cathedral \u2013 a "New Seven Wonders" contender from Russia, protected by UNESCO (viewed from the outside only; entry fee not included).\n- Zaryadye Park \u2013 a unique territory in the historical center with a floating bridge and the flora of all of Russia, built in 2017. You will enjoy the views of the Kremlin.\n- GUM Department Store \u2013 historical trading rows and an architectural masterpiece at Red Square.\n- Nikolskaya Street \u2013 one of the symbols of the 2018 FIFA World Cup in Russia.\n- KGB Headquarters \u2013 where you will hear about one of the most successful secret services in the world.\n- Tverskaya Street, Manezhnaya Square, and Aleksandrovsky Garden.\n- After lunch (not included; the place will be recommended by the guide), you will visit the Kremlin.\n\nInside the Kremlin\u2019s territory, access is from both Kutafya and Trinity Towers. You will see:\n\n- Cathedral Square \u2013 a breathtaking architectural ensemble of the 15th\u201317th centuries, where the lives of Russian grand princes and tsars began and ended, including:\n- The Annunciation Cathedral \u2013 where they were baptized/Christianized.\n- The Assumption Cathedral \u2013 where they were crowned.\nThe Archangel Michael Cathedral \u2013 where they were buried.\n- The Tsar\u2019s Bell and Tsar Cannon \u2013 stunning examples of casting from the 16th\u201318th centuries.\n- The Grand Kremlin Palace \u2013 from an imperial residence to the Russian President\u2019s gala reception quarters.\n- Political and governmental buildings of the Kremlin \u2013 including the Senate, the Palace of Congresses, and the Arsenal.\n- The Kremlin walls and towers \u2013 a unique fortress of medieval Russia.')],e)
