h=A.i(A.n(A.d([j,A.w(a1,A.j("Anuradhapura Anuradhapura, one of the most sacred cities in Sri Lanka, is filled with evocative sights. Famous for its temple ruins, soaring brick towers, enormous dagobas (stupas), and ancient pools, this religious capital is home to the sacred Bodhi tree. Revered as one of Buddhism\u2019s main shrines, the Bodhi Tree here is the oldest surviving tree in the world. Don\u2019t miss the stunning sunset at Ruwanwelisaya, a magnificent stupa adorned with 1,900 elephant figures. The ruins of Lovamahapaya, or the \u2018Brazen Palace,\u2019 covered in bronze tiles, are a must-see, and a visit to the Mihintale mountain peak offers an ethereal view of Anuradhapura.\n\nPolonnaruwa Polonnaruwa, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is an ancient city encircled by three concentric walls. Its majestic ruins, including a royal palace complex, religious buildings, and enormous monuments, cover a vast woodland area. Key monasteries in Polonnaruwa include Rankot Vihara, Menik Vihara, Jetavana, and Alahana Pirivena. Parakrama Samudra, an artificial lake, offers a serene sunset view.\n\nKandy Known as the \u2018Cultural Capital of Sri Lanka,\u2019 Kandy is rich in heritage and culture. The Temple of the Tooth, housing Lord Buddha\u2019s tooth, is one of the most sacred Buddhist shrines. Built in the 17th century, daily rituals performed three times a day add to its charm. The Gadaladeniya Temple showcases Dravidian architecture, and nature lovers will adore the Peradeniya Gardens. The Spice Garden in Kandy offers insights into Ayurveda and indigenous spices. For a memorable sunrise, head to the Knuckle Mountains, featuring 35 peaks and undulating valleys.\n\nKitulgala Kitulgala, a small town and rainforest area, is a haven for adventure seekers. Known as one of the wettest places in Sri Lanka, it offers bird watching, jungle safaris, white-water rafting, waterfall jumps, and jungle walks. The Kelani River, featured in the film \u2018The Bridge on the River Kwai,\u2019 provides a great place to swim and enjoy the river. Kitulgala also offers camping, flat-water rafting, adventure training camps, and waterfall abseiling.\n\nNuwara Eliya Known as \u2018Little England,\u2019 Nuwara Eliya exudes an English village charm with colonial bungalows, rose gardens, and hedgerows. Originally a hill station for Scottish and English pioneers in the tea industry, it offers sports-car hill climbs, horse racing, and Sri Lankan tea experiences.\n\nColombo The capital and largest city of Sri Lanka, Colombo is famous for its colonial heritage, southern beaches, museums, stylish eateries, and galleries. A perfect starting point for your Sri Lanka adventure, Colombo offers plenty to explore, including seafood at Mt Lavinia Beach, the Gangarama Vihara, and leisure activities at the Leisure World amusement park.",a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,A.e(i,a1,a1,l,a1,14,A.b().gh().gi().x,h.w,0,a1,!1),a1,a1,a1,a1),B.k,a1,a1,new A.x(a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,B.l),a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1,a1)],g),A.m(a1,17,a1)),B.e,B.d,B.c,B.b)
